{
  "about": "Orb's starter laboratory catalogue (lis-3). Loaded by services/lab_master_service.py at startup, once, into an empty catalogue, and only while ORB_LAB is on. After that the site's pathologist owns the catalogue and edits it in the laboratory setup screens; this file is never read again for that site. It ships tests, panels, specimen types, sections and rejection reasons. It ships NO reference range and NO critical limit (rulings LIS-R1 and LIS-R2): until a pathologist approves one, a result carries no H or L flag and raises no critical. Capillary ketones, venous and arterial blood gas are bedside tests (performed_at ward_poct, ruling LIS-R18), so they never enter the laboratory's work lists; the laboratory director can reclassify them per site. Every laboratory code in order_sets.json is listed here (tests/test_lab_master.py checks it).",
